# Regular and Special Educators: Handicap Integration Attitudes and Implications for Consultants.

**Authors:** Gans, Karen D.

## Abstract
One-hundred twenty-eight regular and 133 special educators responded to a questionnaire on mainstreaming. The two groups were similiar in their attitudes. Regular educators displayed more negative attitudes, but the differences rarely reached significance. Group differences became more apparent when attitudes concerning specific handicapping conditions were addressed. (Author/CL)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ328162

